      "{**6 NY3d at 525} OPINION OF THE COURT",
      "Defendant was convicted of assault in the second degree and criminal possession of a weapon in the second degree. He was sentenced, as a persistent felony offender, to concurrent indeterminate terms of 20 years to life in prison. The Appellate Division affirmed, relying on People v Geraci (85 NY2d 359 [1995]). A Judge of this Court granted defendant leave to appeal and we now affirm. "
